Hi Luca,

> This patch bumps the zynqmp_zcu102_defconfig to Xilinx release 2022.2.
>=20
> Xilinx 2022.2 includes:
> - U-Boot 2022.01 bug fixes
> - Linux bump to Linux 5.15.36 with bug fixes
> - TF-A 2.6 bug fixes
> - PMUFW bug fixes
>=20
> Signed-off-by: Neal Frager <neal.frager@amd.com>
> ---
>  configs/zynqmp_zcu102_defconfig | 8 ++++----
>  1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
>=20
> diff --git a/configs/zynqmp_zcu102_defconfig=20
> b/configs/zynqmp_zcu102_defconfig index e27dfdb6c9..6047d4299c 100644
> --- a/configs/zynqmp_zcu102_defconfig
> +++ b/configs/zynqmp_zcu102_defconfig
> @@ -5,7 +5,7 @@ BR2_ROOTFS_POST_IMAGE_SCRIPT=3D"board/zynqmp/post-image.s=
h"
>  BR2_ROOTFS_POST_SCRIPT_ARGS=3D"ttyPS0,115200 mmcblk0p2"
>  BR2_LINUX_KERNEL=3Dy
>  BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_CUSTOM_TARBALL=3Dy
> -BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_CUSTOM_TARBALL_LOCATION=3D"$(call github,Xilinx,linux-x=
lnx,xlnx_rebase_v5.15_LTS_2022.1)/xlnx_rebase_v5.15_LTS_2022.1.tar.gz"
> +BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_CUSTOM_TARBALL_LOCATION=3D"$(call github,Xilinx,linux-x=
lnx,xlnx_rebase_v5.15_LTS_2022.2)/xlnx_rebase_v5.15_LTS_2022.2.tar.gz"
>  BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_DEFCONFIG=3D"xilinx_zynqmp"
>  BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_DTS_SUPPORT=3Dy
>  BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_INTREE_DTS_NAME=3D"xilinx/zynqmp-zcu102-rev1.0"
> @@ -15,13 +15,13 @@ BR2_TARGET_ROOTFS_EXT2_4=3Dy  #=20
> BR2_TARGET_ROOTFS_TAR is not set  BR2_TARGET_ARM_TRUSTED_FIRMWARE=3Dy =20
> BR2_TARGET_ARM_TRUSTED_FIRMWARE_CUSTOM_TARBALL=3Dy
> -BR2_TARGET_ARM_TRUSTED_FIRMWARE_CUSTOM_TARBALL_LOCATION=3D"$(call github=
,Xilinx,arm-trusted-firmware,xlnx_rebase_v2.6_2022.1)/xlnx_rebase_v2.6_2022=
.1.tar.gz"
> +BR2_TARGET_ARM_TRUSTED_FIRMWARE_CUSTOM_TARBALL_LOCATION=3D"$(call github=
,Xilinx,arm-trusted-firmware,xlnx_rebase_v2.6_2022.2)/xlnx_rebase_v2.6_2022=
.2.tar.gz"
>  BR2_TARGET_ARM_TRUSTED_FIRMWARE_PLATFORM=3D"zynqmp"
>  BR2_TARGET_ARM_TRUSTED_FIRMWARE_BL31_UBOOT=3Dy
>  BR2_TARGET_UBOOT=3Dy
>  BR2_TARGET_UBOOT_BUILD_SYSTEM_KCONFIG=3Dy
>  BR2_TARGET_UBOOT_CUSTOM_TARBALL=3Dy
> -BR2_TARGET_UBOOT_CUSTOM_TARBALL_LOCATION=3D"$(call github,Xilinx,u-boot-=
xlnx,xlnx_rebase_v2022.01_2022.1)/xlnx_rebase_v2022.01_2022.1.tar.gz"
> +BR2_TARGET_UBOOT_CUSTOM_TARBALL_LOCATION=3D"$(call github,Xilinx,u-boot-=
xlnx,xlnx_rebase_v2022.01_2022.2)/xlnx_rebase_v2022.01_2022.2.tar.gz"
>  BR2_TARGET_UBOOT_BOARD_DEFCONFIG=3D"xilinx_zynqmp_virt"
>  BR2_TARGET_UBOOT_CUSTOM_MAKEOPTS=3D"DEVICE_TREE=3Dzynqmp-zcu102-rev1.0"
>  BR2_TARGET_UBOOT_NEEDS_DTC=3Dy
> @@ -29,7 +29,7 @@ BR2_TARGET_UBOOT_NEEDS_OPENSSL=3Dy =20
> BR2_TARGET_UBOOT_SPL=3Dy  BR2_TARGET_UBOOT_SPL_NAME=3D"spl/boot.bin"
>  BR2_TARGET_UBOOT_ZYNQMP=3Dy
> -BR2_TARGET_UBOOT_ZYNQMP_PMUFW=3D"https://github.com/Xilinx/ubuntu-firmwa=
re/raw/v2022.1_22.04_1/xlnx-firmware/zcu102/zcu102_pmufw.elf"
> +BR2_TARGET_UBOOT_ZYNQMP_PMUFW=3D"https://github.com/nealfrager/buildroot=
-firmware/raw/v2022.2/zcu102/zcu102_pmufw.elf"

> It would be nice to stay on Xilinx official firmwares, but there seem
> to be no 2022.2 firmwares now on the Xilinx repo after Vivado 2022.2
> has been released more than 1 month ago.

I completely agree.  I am in an ongoing discussion within AMD regarding the=
se firmware binaries, and my hope is that an official location will be main=
tained starting with 2023.1.
The firmware repo will cover both zynqmp and versal families.

Once the official location is available, I will be moving the buildroot zyn=
qmp and versal support over to the Xilinx github and deprecating my github.

> One option would be to keep on using a 2022.1 pmufw and upgrade the
> other components. Do you think that would work? I think nowadays the
> interface provided by the PMUFW is quite stable, isn't it?

Yes, we can do this as a temporary solution for the zcu102 and zcu106.  The=
 2022.1 pmufw does work with the other 2022.2 images.

Unfortunately, the kv260 is already using my github since it is not availab=
le anywhere on the Xilinx github yet.

> Should there be good motivations to upgrade to PMUFW 2022.2, let's do
> it with your repo of course.

The only motivation is to have a defconfig where all the components are the=
 same release version.
Functionally, it is not required.

Best regards,
Neal Frager
AMD

